    {
      "id": "0b7a4b0e-1c52-4d4e-9a61-6f1f0d1a0010",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -420,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 380,
        "height": 620,
        "content": "## Google Maps leads with emails, socials and a one-line description\n\n**Who it's for:** agencies, freelancers and sales teams who build local-business lead lists (dentists, restaurants, gyms...).\n\n**What it does:** searches Google Maps, then reads each business website once and adds the email, social profiles, a one-line description and the website's CMS. One row per place goes to Google Sheets.\n\n**Cost (Apify pay-per-event, Sept 2026):** Google Maps Scraper ~$4 per 1,000 places + enrichment $6 per 1,000 websites read. Places without a website, Instagram/Facebook pages used as a website, and dead domains are not charged by the enrichment step. Both Apify nodes have a $1 cost cap; raise it for bigger runs.\n\n**Real test (30 places, Portland/Austin/Munich):** 30/30 rows mapped back by placeId; emails found on 88% of the websites that could be read.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Apify credential (API key or OAuth) to both Apify nodes.\n2. Edit **Search settings**.\n3. Pick your sheet in **Append to Google Sheet** (or delete that node and export the table).\n\nOnly needs emails and socials? Swap the enrichment Actor for `tidytools~website-contact-extractor` ($2 per 1,000 websites)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0b7a4b0e-1c52-4d4e-9a61-6f1f0d1a0011",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        500
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 440,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### Every Google Maps place gets exactly one row\n- no website -> Status `no_website`\n- Instagram/Facebook/Yelp page instead of a website -> `not_a_website` (not read, not charged)\n- chain branches sharing one website -> read once, copied to every branch\n- website redirects to another domain -> Status starts with `check:`\n\nJoin back to the Maps data with **Place ID**."
      }
    }
